{% from "_macros.j2" import todo, places %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ b.brand }}: sales sheet</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
<style>
  /* One A4 page when printed (File > Print > Save as PDF). */
  @page { size: A4; margin: 14mm; }
  .sheet { max-width: 800px; margin: 24px auto; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 36px 40px; }
  .sheet h1 { font-size: 30px; line-height: 1.2; margin: 6px 0 10px; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .sheet .lead { color: var(--muted); font-size: 17px; margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .sheet h2 { font-size: 17px; margin: 22px 0 8px; }
  .sheet .stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; }
  .sheet .stat { padding: 12px 14px; box-shadow: none; }
  .sheet .stat .v { font-size: 26px; }
  .sheet .stat .l { font-size: 14px; }
  .two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; }
  .sheet ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  .sheet li { margin: 4px 0; }
  .contact { margin-top: 22px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-weight: 600; }
  .print-hint { text-align: center; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .two, .sheet .stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .sheet { padding: 24px 18px; } }
  @media print {
    .print-hint { display: none; }
    .sheet { border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0; max-width: none; }
    body { font-size: 13px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<p class="print-hint">To save as a PDF: File, then Print, then "Save as PDF".</p>
<div class="sheet">
  <p class="eyebrow">{{ b.brand }} · for CQC compliance consultancies</p>
  <h1>Your next clients, delivered every Monday.</h1>
  <p class="lead">The care services in your area that have just been rated poorly, just registered with CQC, just
    become due for an inspection, or just been set up as companies, with contact details and the rules for contacting
    each one.</p>

  {% if d.has_numbers %}
  <h2>{{ d.region_name }}, last {{ d.weeks | length }} weeks ({{ d.period }})</h2>
  <div class="stats">
  {% for value, label, note in d.stats() %}
    <div class="stat"><div class="v">{{ value }}</div><div class="l">{{ label }}</div></div>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="two">
    <div>
      <h2>What you get each week</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>New poor ratings</strong>, with the previous rating: services that need an action plan now.</li>
        <li><strong>Newly registered services</strong> facing their first inspection.</li>
        <li><strong>Due for inspection</strong>: ratings 4+ years old, or a year without an inspection. CQC is
          inspecting these first.</li>
        <li><strong>New care companies</strong> that still need to register with CQC.</li>
        <li><strong>Companies now located</strong>: new companies we followed until they showed where they operate.</li>
        <li>The full <strong>never-inspected</strong> and <strong>due-for-inspection</strong> lists for your area.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Why it works</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>First to know: each lead arrives the week it happens, once.</li>
        <li>Official sources: CQC and Companies House, checked every week.</li>
        <li>Ready to use: phone, website and links, plus Excel-ready spreadsheets.</li>
        <li>Independents first: large groups with their own quality teams are left out.</li>
        <li>Compliant: every lead is labelled "email OK", "phone (check TPS/CTPS)" or "post only".</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Price</h2>
  <p>{% if b.price_per_region %}<strong>£{{ "%g" | format(b.price_per_region) }}</strong> {{ b.price_note }}{% else %}{{ todo("price") }}{% endif %}
    {%+ if b.trial %}<strong>{{ b.trial }}</strong>{% endif %} Choose any area in England: a CQC region, councils or postcodes.
    {%+ if b.places_per_area %}{{ places(b) }}{% endif %}
    {%+ if b.exclusive_price %}Or have your area to yourself for <strong>£{{ "%g" | format(b.exclusive_price) }} a month</strong>.{% endif %}</p>

  <div class="contact">
    <span>{{ b.email or todo("your email") }}{% if b.phone %} · {{ b.phone }}{% endif %}</span>
    <span>{{ b.website or todo("your website") }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
